# CreepToDock.srv
#
# Laser-guided final approach into the charging dock.  The mission
# supervisor calls this AFTER it has navigated to the dock approach pose
# (the pose ``approach_back`` metres south of the dock centre).  The
# controller then drives the robot forward at ``creep_speed`` until the
# front laser reads below ``creep_stop_range`` (robot seated), or until it
# detects a stall / timeout.
#
# The same service is implemented by the simulator and the real dock
# controller, so the supervisor's docking logic is hardware-agnostic.

# (empty request — all geometry comes from ROS parameters)

---
# True when the robot ended pressed against the dock (front clearance <
# creep_stop_range, or a stall / flat-clearance condition fired).
bool seated
# Front laser clearance (m) at the moment the service returned; -1 when no
# scan was available.
float32 front_clearance_m